sprd_wlan_combo: one WCN power transition at a time; an RX interrupt without a context is dropped, not a panic

power_cnt is atomic, the transitions behind it are not. The probe powers the chip off after it registered wlan0,
outside RTNL, so userspace (hostapd, netifd) can open the interface meanwhile: the open's power-on ran
start_marlin + post_init while the probe's power-off was still in post_deinit, which then cleared the channels and
sc2355_hif.hif that post_init had just set; the next RX interrupt read hif->rx_mgmt from NULL in hard IRQ
(pcie_rx_handle+0x34, "paging request at 00000000000030b8", seen under 6.18 in FINDINGS 31n; the 5.4 driver has
the same code). sprd_iface_set_power holds a mutex across the transition; pcie_rx_handle drops a list that
arrives with no context and logs it once; the context pointer is published with release/acquire.
On the way: probe's error paths and remove powered off after sprd_core_free had freed hif (now before), and a
power-on that failed in post_init or the version sync left the chip started, and after a failed sync the
channels registered, with the count at 0 (now undone as a power-off does).

